{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1182185-umbral-homelands","id":1182185,"title":"Umbral Homelands","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-03T22:52:11-08:00","id":1182185,"title":"Umbral Homelands","content":"So all the Werewolf Tribes have Homeland Realms in the Umbra. Even the Croatan's still exists though is empty; and the White Howlers' has been overturned into a toxic hellpit by the Black Spiral Dancers. Only the Silent Striders' and Bunyip's are currently lost.<br /> <br /> W20 Umbra also discusses Coyote Tunnel, which essentially serves as a Nuwisha Homeland, and the great tree that is the Corax Homeland (i call it Austras Koks, Latvian &quot;Tree of the Dawn&quot;).<br /> <br /> I was pondering what other such spirit realms might exist.<br /> <br /> - Should the Hakkan have their own Tribal Homeland? Some sort of romanticized vision of Japan that mixes Edo culture with actively dueling Samurai of earlier eras? Or are some of the fortresses in the Shadow Lord Homeland distinctly Japanese in architecture, from where Hakken Daimyos send their Samurai out to war against the armies of other Daimyos and Shadow Lords over the Great Mountain?<br /> <br /> - Same question for the Boli Zouhsize! Separate umbral Homeland, where a distinctly Chinese city is kept in utopian social order by upholding Confucian principles? Or do their skyscrapers stand side by side with the Solar-Punk future-tech utopia of the Glass Walkers?<br /> <br /> - Same question for the Kucha Ekundu! Is there a separate realm from the overgrown hunter's paradise of the Red Talons, that's an African savanna untouched by humans?<br /> <br /> - Same question for the Siberakh! Though in their case I lean most strongly toward no access to any Tribal Homeland at all (yet?)<br /> <br /> That covers the Garou, so now lets look at the other Changing Breeds....<br /> <br /> Bastet have their Den-Realms rather than shared Tribal Homelands, the Nagah have Ananta, and Ananasi have the Sylie. Fair enough. It does strike me as a bit of a loss that we don't have a Balam Homeland with Mesoamerican pyramids rising out of a rainforest, but I take the thematic point of how much more individualist the Bastet are in their spirituality than the Garou.<br /> <br /> So regarding Breeds with as strong an inbuilt tie to the Umbra as the Garou, that leaves the Ajaba, the Kitsune, and the Ratkin.<br /> <br /> With the Kitsune, obviously the easiest answer would be if they didn't get one because of how young they are. That said, I've considered the possibility (and this could resolve the issue for the Hakken as well) that the &quot;Temple of the Ancestors&quot; in the original Hengeyokai book could metaphysically serve as a collective &quot;Umbral Homeland&quot; for the Beast Courts.<br /> <br /> The Ajaba having a realm would be nice as it would provide an African motif realm that none of the Garou realms do (the Silent Strider Homeland has/had an Ancient Egyptian motif, but it's currently lost, and the Ajaba realm would probably be more sub-saharan African as their central homeland). However this too could be something that was lost to them when the Endless Storm's massacre, but they're working to reclaim it.<br /> <br /> The handful of &quot;Paradise Realms&quot; mentioned in the original Ratkin book probably fill this niche. The Ratkin which is the real Homeland Rat intends for them. Too say nothing of wherever the hell the Munchmausen are coming from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T10:35:57-08:00","id":1182311,"title":"","content":"Tribes and Tribal Homelands are all dependent on their Totem.<br /> <br /> So all members of the tribe have the same tribal homeland regardless of the differences in human cultures their homids grew up in. Time differences are probably more jarring to modern homids than different cultures in the same time. The vast majority of Garou would have lived in Stone Age times. Hakken are Shadow Lords, Boli Zousizhe are Glass Walkers, etc. so they are all in the same homeland. (I think it's just silly to say they have the same totem, but are somehow different tribes). Homelands should reflect the tribal culture from the totem, not the ephemeral human culture some members come from. There's fairy tale logic to the homelands, so there is no problem with blending disparate elements together. So it is fine with the Shadow Lord homeland having a large place for Stone Age cultures on foot alongside horse riding barbarians with bronze and iron weapons along with various castle types from Eastern Europe to Japan. But what is more important is the brooding sense of a sudden storm that could erupt at any moment and torrential rains fall while lightning flashes and thunder shakes the trees and grass.<br /> <br /> I ignore the Siberakh, but if they did show up in my games, they'd have their own homeland because they have their own Totem. It might not be very big because of relatively few numbers.<br /> <br /> Homelands are there basically to explain where the Ancestor spirits reside, right? So as long as a breed has Ancestors, there should probably be some kind of homeland even if it is distant and mysterious for other reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T18:01:33-08:00","id":1182451,"title":"","content":"I can definitely see the Boli Zouhisze seemlessly fitting in the Glass Walker Homeland, and Kucha Ekundu in the Red Talon one. What definitely does not seem to be the case though is that there are Hakken in the Shadow Lord homeland, given that the two branches don't consider themselves the same Tribe. And this line from the W20 Umbra book makes it sound like the Homeland missing an ancient link between the two means the Hakken aren't also present.<br /> &quot;To the north is a forbidding sea where legend tells of a great kingdom of ancestor-spirits on the far shore, who gave rise to both the modern tribe and their Hakken cousins.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm leaning right now toward the &quot;Temple of the Ancestors&quot; filling that role for the Beast Courts covers the Hakken for the most part, hence their comparative spiritual removal from the Homeland where Grandfather Thunder dwells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T20:06:50-08:00","id":1182481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1182185-umbral-homelands?p=1182451#post1182451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can definitely see the Boli Zouhisze seemlessly fitting in the Glass Walker Homeland, and Kucha Ekundu in the Red Talon one. What definitely does not seem to be the case though is that there are Hakken in the Shadow Lord homeland, given that the two branches don't consider themselves the same Tribe. And this line from the W20 Umbra book makes it sound like the Homeland missing an ancient link between the two means the Hakken aren't also present.<br /> &quot;To the north is a forbidding sea where legend tells of a great kingdom of ancestor-spirits on the far shore, who gave rise to both the modern tribe and their Hakken cousins.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm leaning right now toward the &quot;Temple of the Ancestors&quot; filling that role for the Beast Courts covers the Hakken for the most part, hence their comparative spiritual removal from the Homeland where Grandfather Thunder dwells.</div> </div> </div> </div>W20 forgot about how the Revised Tribebook mentioned at least one other branch of the tribe's roots, the portion of the tribe that resides in Central Asia. Which would suggest a seamless continuum, as they've been noted as living from Iberia all the way into Russia for a while, with an established history to boot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T20:14:34-08:00","id":1182485,"title":"","content":"As far as I know though, the Iberian and Central Asian Shadow Lords regard themselves as part of the same Tribe as the more famous Carpathian Shadow Lords. The Hakken and the Shadow Lords though have always counted themselves as unrelated save for the same patron Incarna.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T22:05:55-08:00","id":1182499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1182185-umbral-homelands?p=1182485#post1182485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I know though, the Iberian and Central Asian Shadow Lords regard themselves as part of the same Tribe as the more famous Carpathian Shadow Lords. The Hakken and the Shadow Lords though have always counted themselves as unrelated save for the same patron Incarna.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so, the Central Asian branch, per the Revised tribebook. It was just low key about noting this, which of course means that it got lost in the noise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T23:16:24-08:00","id":1182509,"title":"","content":"I guess the biggest question in the standard of Tribal Homelands tying to a Tribal Totem - is that the Black Spiral Dancers don't have a specific Tribal Totem, but still have an Umbral Homeland. Of course it once tied to Lion, but he fled millennia ago*. <br /> <br /> I'm leaning toward the idea that those Bane Totems that originate from the Wyrm primarily manifest their Incarna forms in Malfeas, but those who are fallen once-Gaian Totems are more closely tied to the Dancer Homeland, with Wippoorwill as the first among them - but Bat's fallen aspect grows stronger to oppose her.<br /> <br /> *seemingly demoted in power by the fall of the White Howlers, he's generally a member of Griffin's Brood now; so most likely found in the Red Talon Homeland if you're looking for the full blown Lion Incarna himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T16:22:41-08:00","id":1182741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1182185-umbral-homelands?p=1182311#post1182311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Homelands are there basically to explain where the Ancestor spirits reside, right? So as long as a breed has Ancestors, there should probably be some kind of homeland even if it is distant and mysterious for other reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I expect Gaia would provide homelands for the spirits of all fera to go to after their physical bodies die, but some of these homelands may be forgotten, lost, or simply inaccessible to the Garou. Unless a source book specifies that a certain group <i>doesn't</i> have a homeland, I'd want to say it's out there, and at worst simply unknown or unreachable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T23:45:33-08:00","id":1183848,"title":"","content":"I've decided the &quot;Valley of Tears&quot; is the Ajaba Homeland. It's a place where emenations of all those slain by the Ajaba have rest as bones, while being reborn as elemental spirits, bringing rain and fertility to the immense African valley.<br /> <br /> Since the massacre of the Ajaba by the Enldess Storm though, the Realm has been in unending monsoon/hurricane conditions without any Ajaba Ancestor Spirit or Totem to be found. The most powerful aspect of the Hyena Incarna anyone has been able to find is the scavanger spirit hanging with Rat with the Bone Gnawer Homeland.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-09-2018, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-09T08:13:20-08:00","id":1183938,"title":"","content":"The Silent Striders homeland still exists and, as of revised, could be found as part of an epic quest (the sort of thing about on par with finding the Silver Crown). What it looks like is described in Wepahwet's write up in the back of the revised tribe-book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}